            "instructions": "Work through the following in order, writing your steps and answers. 1) Current and voltage: state what current and voltage measure, their units, and the relationship V = IR for a simple resistor. Solve one example: a 12 V source across a 4 ohm resistor; find the current. 2) Series circuits: state the rules (same current, voltages add, R_total = R1 + R2 + ...). Solve one example: a 12 V source with 2 ohm and 4 ohm resistors in series; find total resistance, current, and voltage across each resistor. 3) Parallel circuits: state the rules (same voltage across branches, currents add, 1/R_total = 1/R1 + 1/R2 + ...). Solve one example: a 12 V source with 6 ohm and 3 ohm resistors in parallel; find total resistance, current through each branch, and total current. 4) Mixed circuits: reduce a circuit with a series part and a parallel part step by step. Example: a 12 V source with a 2 ohm resistor in series with a parallel pair of 6 ohm and 3 ohm resistors; find total resistance, total current, voltage across the parallel pair, and current through each parallel branch. 5) Self-check: rework the mixed-circuit example from scratch without looking at your first solution, then compare and correct any errors. If you cannot correct an error, note exactly which step failed and why.",
