            "scopeRef": "scope_2",
            "disposition": "INCLUDED",
            "contribution": "The concrete CSV totals report that applies loops and dictionaries to a real file and provides the first useful checkpoint."
          }
        ],
        "activities": [
          {
            "localId": "csv_totals_work",
            "outcomeRefs": [
              "csv_totals"
            ],
            "scopeRefs": [
              "scope_1",
              "scope_2"
            ],
            "title": "Build and check a CSV totals report using loops and dictionaries",
            "activityType": "Guided programming task with independent changed example",
            "purpose": "Teach the shared loops/dictionaries prerequisite through the actual CSV report, then verify it with a changed CSV example so plan_2 can rely on the same prerequisite without repeating it.",
            "instructions": "Use a supplied small CSV file with columns such as date, category, amount. First, read the file row by row and print each row so you can see the data. Then write a loop that accumulates a total per category in a dictionary. Print the dictionary of totals. Check the totals by adding the amounts for one category by hand and comparing. Next, change the CSV file to a new small example with different categories and amounts, and run the same report to confirm it still produces correct totals. During the work, explain in your own words what the loop does on each row and how the dictionary stores the running totals. If a total is wrong, find the actual line or step that caused the error and correct it, then rerun. Stop when the report produces correct totals for both the original and the changed CSV file and you can explain the loop and dictionary steps.",
            "completionCriterion": "The CSV totals report runs on the supplied CSV file and on a changed CSV example, produces correct totals for both, and the learner can explain the loop and dictionary steps used.",
            "effort": {
              "lowMinutes": 45,
              "likelyMinutes": 75,
              "highMinutes": 120
            },
            "timeboxMinutes": 90,
            "commitment": {
              "category": "COMMITTED"
            },
            "hardDependencies": []
          }
        ],
